Here is the root cause:
The original implementation of `phy_start_aneg` did not properly manage the PHY lock, which could lead to race conditions or inconsistent states when multiple functions attempted to access or modify the PHY device's settings concurrently. This lack of locking could result in unexpected behavior or failures when auto-negotiation was initiated while other operations were being performed on the same PHY device.

